Paul is right, it is time for a sign of life.

The development team, and the porting sub-groups, have been working
intensively on the development of version 3.1.  There is no slack, and
there is no lull in the teams' activities.

NetHack 3.1 is radically different from 3.0, and it involved major re-writes
of large sections of the code.  The amount of time required to finish it is
dictated primarily by the number, nature, and scope of problems encountered
along the way.  The team has been working on it, literally, day-in and 
day-out for the last year and a half.

We understand the impatience, but we don't think it will be wise for us to
commit ourselves to a date of release until we are fairly certain that we
can deliver.  We are not at such a point yet.  All we can say at this point
is that NetHack 3.1 exists, and that it is worth waiting for its completion.
It would be easy to say "soon", but the truth is that we can't exactly say
yet how soon is "soon."  Please be patient with us a while longer.

For the development team,

-Izchak


